1
00:00:04,237 --> 00:00:05,705
MICHIKO DAIMON
FREELANCE SURGEON

2
00:00:09,709 --> 00:00:11,378
Whoa!

3
00:00:11,878 --> 00:00:13,279
Ouch!

4
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:15,281
It hurts!

5
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:16,850
- What's wrong?
- It hurts!

6
00:00:16,916 --> 00:00:18,685
It hurts?

7
00:00:18,752 --> 00:00:20,520
- How bad does it hurt?
- It hurts.

8
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,592
It hurts that bad?

9
00:00:27,761 --> 00:00:29,295
Where's your mom?

10
00:00:31,631 --> 00:00:34,034
- What a pain.
- Ouch!

11
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,902
Are you his mom?

12
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:44,978
Hey,

13
00:00:45,045 --> 00:00:46,679
haven't we met before?

14
00:00:46,746 --> 00:00:47,747
Haven't we?

15
00:00:48,248 --> 00:00:49,883
Ouch! It hurts!

16
00:00:49,949 --> 00:00:52,352
- Oh, no. Now he's crying.
- Ko-chan?

17
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:53,586
Ko-chan! What happened?

18
00:00:53,653 --> 00:00:56,556
- You're his mom?
- What did you do to my son?

19
00:00:56,623 --> 00:00:58,191
- She made him cry.
- What?

20
00:00:59,793 --> 00:01:01,161
It wasn't me.

21
00:01:02,028 --> 00:01:05,732
- Dr. Daimon! What have you done?
- It figures you did this!

22
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:09,302
How could you hurt this sweet child?
You really are a demon!

23
00:01:09,369 --> 00:01:11,671
- Shut up!
- Ouch! That hurt!

24
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,673
And you, quit your crying!

25
00:01:14,674 --> 00:01:16,176
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

26
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:19,145
You're even making his mom cry!
You're so abusive!

27
00:01:19,212 --> 00:01:20,747
- That's right!
- Are you okay?

28
00:01:20,814 --> 00:01:22,248
- It hurts!
- Let me see it.

29
00:01:22,315 --> 00:01:24,284
- Let me see it.
- You'll be okay.

30
00:01:25,185 --> 00:01:26,486
Isn't she…

31
00:01:28,688 --> 00:01:32,459
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

32
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,829
<i>2021.</i>

33
00:01:35,895 --> 00:01:38,998
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

34
00:01:39,065 --> 00:01:41,568
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

35
00:01:42,969 --> 00:01:44,637
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>

36
00:01:44,704 --> 00:01:47,073
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

37
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:50,243
<i>have somehow weathered the storm.</i>

38
00:01:51,244 --> 00:01:52,078
<i>However,</i>

39
00:01:52,145 --> 00:01:53,913
<i>the university hospital's once illustrious</i>

40
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:56,783
<i>Surgery Department was moved</i>
<i>to the branch hospital.</i>

41
00:01:56,850 --> 00:01:59,352
<i>The number of surgeries</i>
<i>was greatly decreased</i>

42
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:02,255
<i>and it was running in the red.</i>

43
00:02:03,223 --> 00:02:04,491
Silence!

44
00:02:08,261 --> 00:02:11,598
The structure of this hospital
is being revised.

45
00:02:11,664 --> 00:02:12,932
As of today,

46
00:02:12,999 --> 00:02:17,203
it has been made better
as the Medical Solutions Division!

47
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:22,041
GENGORO YAJIMA, MEDICAL INTERN
RISA ABUKAWA, MEDICAL INTERN

48
00:02:22,108 --> 00:02:24,377
Internal medicine methods
will take priority,

49
00:02:24,444 --> 00:02:29,849
while Surgery will perform surgeries
in accordance with those methods.

50
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:31,885
I look forward to your cooperation.

51
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:38,291
I look forward to your cooperation!

52
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:47,967
From now on, Dr. Korogi
will be head of surgeries.

53
00:02:55,542 --> 00:02:57,577
Awesome.

54
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:04,918
We will now conduct a laparoscopic
lower anterior resection.

55
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:07,253
Watch carefully, interns.

56
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,122
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

57
00:03:09,189 --> 00:03:12,225
Is this your first laparoscopic surgery?

58
00:03:12,725 --> 00:03:14,160
Yes.

59
00:03:14,227 --> 00:03:16,496
Now, don't be so nervous.

60
00:03:16,563 --> 00:03:20,366
What's important in surgery
is appropriate focus, and "relax".

61
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:23,303
Appropriate focus, and relax?

62
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:26,206
No. It's "relax."

63
00:03:26,272 --> 00:03:27,707
Relax.

64
00:03:28,474 --> 00:03:30,710
You, play some music. Something light.

65
00:03:30,777 --> 00:03:32,712
That is not the job of a surgical nurse.

66
00:03:36,583 --> 00:03:39,619
I want to see your
amazing skills, Head Doctor.

67
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:41,821
Scalpel…

68
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:50,930
Bov…

69
00:04:05,144 --> 00:04:06,246
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

70
00:04:06,312 --> 00:04:08,881
<i>this freelance maverick doctor</i>

71
00:04:09,449 --> 00:04:13,820
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

72
00:04:13,886 --> 00:04:17,123
- Pringle is ready. Metz.
- Here.

73
00:04:17,190 --> 00:04:18,992
<i>She hates groups,</i>

74
00:04:19,058 --> 00:04:22,061
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

75
00:04:22,128 --> 00:04:24,030
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

76
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:27,567
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

77
00:04:27,634 --> 00:04:29,702
<i>to work her way up.</i>

78
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:32,739
Rectum anastomosis ready.

79
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,348
It's hard.

80
00:04:45,918 --> 00:04:49,489
Depending on the thickness
and toughness of the tissue,

81
00:04:49,555 --> 00:04:51,858
the automated anastomosis cutter
won't work.

82
00:04:52,825 --> 00:04:57,063
But as long as you figure out
how to make it work…

83
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:00,900
See?

84
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,368
That did it.

85
00:05:02,435 --> 00:05:03,836
This is a lucky patient.

86
00:05:04,604 --> 00:05:07,507
Thanks to your great skills,
the procedure didn't have to change.

87
00:05:08,207 --> 00:05:10,476
You sure know your stuff.

88
00:05:10,543 --> 00:05:11,611
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

89
00:05:15,448 --> 00:05:16,482
There.

90
00:05:18,084 --> 00:05:20,186
I suggest manually suturing
the anastomosis.

91
00:05:22,855 --> 00:05:25,191
I haven't seen you before.
Are you a part-timer?

92
00:05:25,258 --> 00:05:27,026
I'm a freelance nurse.

93
00:05:27,093 --> 00:05:28,761
Don't mind that, Head Doctor.

94
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:30,330
Continue the surgery.

95
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:40,440
Your ligation is slow!

96
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:43,109
- I can't see what I'm doing!
- Sorry.

97
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:45,111
Uh-oh. Suction.

98
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:47,447
Suction. Right.

99
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:49,649
Not there! Here!

100
00:05:49,716 --> 00:05:52,218
- Hurry up!
- You're going too fast!

101
00:05:52,285 --> 00:05:54,687
Quit grumbling and move, dummy!

102
00:05:54,754 --> 00:05:56,956
- "Dummy?"
- Dr. Daimon, that's verbal abuse.

103
00:05:59,125 --> 00:06:01,361
Abuse is good for you, dummy!

104
00:06:01,427 --> 00:06:02,428
Dummy!

105
00:06:02,495 --> 00:06:04,464
- Hurry up!
- Yes, ma'am!

106
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:06,466
- Kelly.
- Here.

107
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:09,268
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

108
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:14,307
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

109
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:16,376
- That's wrong! Are you deaf?
- Sorry!

110
00:06:30,757 --> 00:06:32,291
One moment, please.

111
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:41,834
What? It's still this early?

112
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:45,138
I could still do 12 or 13 more.

113
00:06:45,204 --> 00:06:47,306
You really are fast, Dr. Daimon.

114
00:06:47,373 --> 00:06:50,309
- You were magnificent again today.
- Thank you.

115
00:06:50,376 --> 00:06:51,711
Goodbye.

116
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:54,347
OPERATING ROOM 1

117
00:06:56,582 --> 00:06:57,650
Nurse station!

118
00:06:57,717 --> 00:07:01,053
<i>Get me a new surgical nurse right away!</i>

119
00:07:01,554 --> 00:07:02,722
Right away?

120
00:07:03,689 --> 00:07:04,891
Who is it?

121
00:07:04,957 --> 00:07:06,492
<i>Head Doctor Korogi!</i>

122
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:10,096
All the nurses are busy.

123
00:07:10,163 --> 00:07:11,264
Do it yourself.

124
00:07:11,330 --> 00:07:13,332
<i>- Are you crazy?</i>
- Are you?

125
00:07:13,399 --> 00:07:15,868
Sorry! I'll be there right away!

126
00:07:23,075 --> 00:07:25,945
Arrogantly shoving instruments in my face
is throwing me off!

127
00:07:26,479 --> 00:07:28,214
Where's the new surgical nurse?

128
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:31,584
- You're late!
- I'm sorry.

129
00:07:31,651 --> 00:07:33,753
- Take over!
- Certainly, sir.

130
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:36,756
You call that an obedient attitude?

131
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:44,931
- Let's continue.
- Yes, sir.

132
00:07:44,997 --> 00:07:46,499
4-0 braided.

133
00:07:47,266 --> 00:07:48,901
What? Braided?

134
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:50,536
Don't you want a mono?

135
00:07:50,603 --> 00:07:52,772
BRAIDED, MONOFILAMENT

136
00:07:56,509 --> 00:07:59,045
- What's your problem? Give it!
- Yes, sir!

137
00:08:00,246 --> 00:08:01,247
Here.

138
00:08:32,445 --> 00:08:35,181
Anastomosis reinforcement complete.
Time to close.

139
00:08:35,248 --> 00:08:36,382
Time out!

140
00:08:39,552 --> 00:08:41,587
How dare you keep interfering?

141
00:08:41,654 --> 00:08:42,788
What's your problem?

142
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:44,590
We're one gauze short.

143
00:08:45,157 --> 00:08:46,058
What?

144
00:08:46,125 --> 00:08:47,393
I checked them all.

145
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:48,761
It must be on the floor.

146
00:08:48,828 --> 00:08:50,596
I have checked everywhere already.

147
00:08:50,663 --> 00:08:52,331
The gauze is in the surgical area.

148
00:08:52,398 --> 00:08:54,000
Probably under the anastomosis.

149
00:08:54,066 --> 00:08:55,801
- Grasping forceps.
- Here.

150
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:57,637
- Let's check anyway.
- Yes, sir.

151
00:09:07,246 --> 00:09:08,614
There's the gauze!

152
00:09:19,058 --> 00:09:21,160
I knew it was her.

153
00:09:28,134 --> 00:09:31,103
So you're still a freelancer, right?

154
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:34,740
You're as unpleasant as ever.

155
00:09:34,807 --> 00:09:37,109
I don't know who you are. Goodbye.

156
00:09:37,176 --> 00:09:38,444
Oh, wow.

157
00:09:40,379 --> 00:09:44,350
There's a woman more unpleasant
than you? That's amazing.

158
00:09:45,918 --> 00:09:47,186
Serves you right.

159
00:09:48,988 --> 00:09:50,923
MACCHAN DINER
50 YEN OFF

160
00:09:51,624 --> 00:09:54,093
"Macchan Diner, 50 yen off."

161
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,828
That's good for 50 yen off?

162
00:09:55,895 --> 00:09:57,430
Hey, thief. Wait!

163
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,933
And what about this freelance nurse?

164
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,168
Oh, yes.

165
00:10:02,234 --> 00:10:05,438
Ten years ago, I operated with her once.

166
00:10:05,504 --> 00:10:06,505
Where?

167
00:10:06,572 --> 00:10:08,908
On the ship back from Cuba,
there was a patient.

168
00:10:08,975 --> 00:10:09,809
Right.

169
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:13,346
You remember the face of a nurse
you only ever saw once?

170
00:10:13,412 --> 00:10:16,148
- That really is unusual.
- Freelance nurses

171
00:10:16,215 --> 00:10:18,484
<i>are pretty common overseas.</i>

172
00:10:18,551 --> 00:10:21,120
<i>Unless they're really good,</i>
<i>they don't last.</i>

173
00:10:21,187 --> 00:10:22,388
<i>She's talented?</i>

174
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:24,824
Yes, she was pretty skilled.

175
00:10:24,890 --> 00:10:26,225
Really?

176
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:29,695
<i>If she's good enough</i>
<i>for you to remember her,</i>

177
00:10:29,762 --> 00:10:31,697
<i>- I would like to meet her.</i>
<i>- I would like it, too!</i>

178
00:10:31,764 --> 00:10:34,100
I hope we can work together.

179
00:10:34,166 --> 00:10:39,772
What? Well, I'll admit she's a good nurse,
but her personality is awful.

180
00:10:39,839 --> 00:10:41,173
Her personality is awful?

181
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:42,875
She never smiles,

182
00:10:42,942 --> 00:10:45,645
never says "hi," she's arrogant,
and always looks mad.

183
00:10:46,178 --> 00:10:48,814
- That's you!
- That's you, Ms. Daimon.

184
00:10:48,881 --> 00:10:51,050
- That's you, Michiko.
- It is not!

185
00:10:51,117 --> 00:10:53,853
My interest in meeting her
is getting piqued.

186
00:10:53,919 --> 00:10:55,888
If she came to work for me,

187
00:10:55,955 --> 00:11:00,660
I would have a surgeon,
anesthetists, and even a nurse!

188
00:11:00,726 --> 00:11:02,862
All right! Then I can operate with her!

189
00:11:02,928 --> 00:11:04,697
Yes. Oh…

190
00:11:04,764 --> 00:11:05,965
I don't need <i>minami.</i>

191
00:11:06,032 --> 00:11:08,634
You discarded a <i>minami</i> tile, Michiko?

192
00:11:08,701 --> 00:11:10,503
<i>- Ron!</i>
- Really?

193
00:11:10,569 --> 00:11:11,737
Look!

194
00:11:11,804 --> 00:11:14,640
- A triplet of four winds!
- Oh, wow!

195
00:11:14,707 --> 00:11:18,611
How did that happen?
You were missing some tiles!

196
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:20,546
How many years have you played this?

197
00:11:21,781 --> 00:11:24,050
SURGERY BRANCH

198
00:11:25,751 --> 00:11:28,187
Are you really sure you checked?

199
00:11:28,254 --> 00:11:29,221
Yes.

200
00:11:29,288 --> 00:11:31,057
Then this wouldn't happen!

201
00:11:31,123 --> 00:11:31,957
What's wrong?

202
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:34,794
A drill bit broke in a surgery
the other day.

203
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,697
A fragment from it was found in an x-ray.

204
00:11:39,632 --> 00:11:41,000
Uh-oh.

205
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:43,502
I'll do it next time.
I won't screw up like this.

206
00:11:43,569 --> 00:11:44,403
"Screw up?"

207
00:11:44,470 --> 00:11:45,538
I did not screw up!

208
00:11:45,604 --> 00:11:46,439
Hey.

209
00:11:46,505 --> 00:11:49,175
Leave this to me, the Head of Surgery.

210
00:11:49,241 --> 00:11:50,443
Yes, sir.

211
00:11:50,509 --> 00:11:53,446
You part-timers ganging up
and nit-picking?

212
00:11:53,512 --> 00:11:55,014
- We're freelancers!
- We're freelancers!

213
00:11:55,081 --> 00:11:57,450
Damn. That's really annoying.

214
00:11:57,516 --> 00:11:59,719
Your attitude and height are way outsized!

215
00:11:59,785 --> 00:12:01,854
- That's ad hominem.
- Sorry.

216
00:12:01,921 --> 00:12:05,925
I'll check this out and report it
to Acting Director Hiruma.

217
00:12:05,991 --> 00:12:09,161
Excuse me. Acting Director Hiruma
is out on a business trip.

218
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:11,697
- What?
- He's at a conference in Hakone.

219
00:12:11,764 --> 00:12:12,832
Hakone?

220
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:15,301
Visiting hot springs at a time like this?

221
00:12:15,367 --> 00:12:17,103
Surgeons sure are vain. Bye.

222
00:12:17,169 --> 00:12:18,070
What's with him?

223
00:12:18,137 --> 00:12:20,773
Hot springs? That would be nice.

224
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:22,775
I'll go with Akira.

225
00:12:22,842 --> 00:12:24,176
And never come back!

226
00:12:24,243 --> 00:12:25,845
- Ouch!
- Oops!

227
00:12:25,911 --> 00:12:28,748
- What's your problem?
- I'm so sorry!

228
00:12:28,814 --> 00:12:32,284
Mr. Itsuki in room 502 is in intense pain.

229
00:12:33,285 --> 00:12:34,386
Please come.

230
00:12:35,154 --> 00:12:36,455
I'm sorry.

231
00:12:38,491 --> 00:12:39,759
Maybe we should go, too.

232
00:12:40,493 --> 00:12:41,460
Let's go.

233
00:12:45,698 --> 00:12:47,733
- It still hurts?
- Yes, it hurts.

234
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:50,569
Doctor, will my husband be all right?

235
00:12:50,636 --> 00:12:52,605
Possible abscess in the pelvic cavity.

236
00:12:52,671 --> 00:12:54,440
- Do a CT scan right away.
- Right.

237
00:12:54,507 --> 00:12:56,909
- Excuse me.
- We'll get you up. Excuse me.

238
00:13:00,646 --> 00:13:03,249
- Let's go.
- Who said you could do that?

239
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:06,185
Mr. Itsuki, I will perform the tests.

240
00:13:06,252 --> 00:13:07,720
I can't leave him to you.

241
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:10,322
Dr. Daimon, he is my patient.

242
00:13:10,389 --> 00:13:12,491
What did you do in that surgery?

243
00:13:13,492 --> 00:13:15,027
The surgery went perfectly.

244
00:13:15,728 --> 00:13:17,596
You saw it, right?

245
00:13:17,663 --> 00:13:19,198
Yes.

246
00:13:19,265 --> 00:13:21,000
Dr. Korogi's surgery was perfect.

247
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:26,539
It will be okay.
We'll do some tests just in case.

248
00:13:28,707 --> 00:13:29,542
Give me a hand.

249
00:13:29,608 --> 00:13:31,043
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

250
00:13:45,524 --> 00:13:47,459
What are the CT results?

251
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:49,195
Dr. Daimon…

252
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:55,801
Tell me now!

253
00:13:59,238 --> 00:14:00,206
That's abuse!

254
00:14:00,272 --> 00:14:01,907
Abuse is good for you!

255
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:04,944
Tell me!

256
00:14:05,578 --> 00:14:07,413
It was just like you said.

257
00:14:07,479 --> 00:14:10,149
There's an abscess in his pelvic cavity.

258
00:14:10,716 --> 00:14:12,284
I knew it!

259
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,053
We need to operate again.

260
00:14:14,119 --> 00:14:16,355
But Dr. Korogi…

261
00:14:16,422 --> 00:14:18,591
If he does it, he'll blow it again!

262
00:14:18,657 --> 00:14:20,960
"Again?"
You mean his surgery was a failure?

263
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:25,331
Weren't you the one who said
it was perfect? Weren't you watching?

264
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:30,135
Around the head doctor,
I thought it was best to say that.

265
00:14:30,736 --> 00:14:31,837
Oops.

266
00:14:33,005 --> 00:14:34,473
What about you two?

267
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:39,311
I was only suctioning around the edges.
I couldn't see.

268
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:41,247
It was my first time. I was so nervous,

269
00:14:41,313 --> 00:14:43,716
I had no idea
what the head doctor was doing.

270
00:14:43,782 --> 00:14:44,783
Unbelievable.

271
00:14:45,818 --> 00:14:47,486
You're all hopeless.

272
00:14:48,954 --> 00:14:49,822
Right!

273
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:52,057
But there should be
a video of the surgery!

274
00:14:52,124 --> 00:14:54,627
That's right! Video for the records!

275
00:14:55,494 --> 00:14:57,363
Video of a surgery?

276
00:14:58,097 --> 00:14:59,598
One moment, please.

277
00:15:01,433 --> 00:15:02,568
Hey.

278
00:15:02,635 --> 00:15:04,103
Hey, you there.

279
00:15:04,803 --> 00:15:07,139
You were kicked out
during that surgery, right?

280
00:15:09,341 --> 00:15:10,476
How come?

281
00:15:11,343 --> 00:15:12,411
It was nothing.

282
00:15:12,478 --> 00:15:14,713
I simply made the doctor angry.

283
00:15:15,681 --> 00:15:19,551
Unfortunately, there's no video
of Mr. Itsuki's surgery.

284
00:15:19,618 --> 00:15:21,053
That's not possible!

285
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:23,889
NO VIDEO

286
00:15:23,956 --> 00:15:26,625
What? Then someone deleted it?

287
00:15:27,192 --> 00:15:31,196
- I don't know.
- No. That surgery wasn't filmed.

288
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:34,366
We're all very busy. Will that be all?

289
00:15:38,904 --> 00:15:40,539
Did you recall something?

290
00:15:41,407 --> 00:15:42,741
No, I didn't.

291
00:15:47,513 --> 00:15:48,948
Dr. Korogi,

292
00:15:49,481 --> 00:15:51,684
the reason I summoned you from abroad was…

293
00:15:52,351 --> 00:15:57,189
because I believed you could help
with my chemical surgery program.

294
00:15:57,756 --> 00:15:58,824
Yes.

295
00:16:00,559 --> 00:16:05,364
There are many risks involved in surgery.

296
00:16:05,431 --> 00:16:06,432
Therefore,

297
00:16:06,498 --> 00:16:09,501
surgeries should be kept to a minimum.

298
00:16:10,235 --> 00:16:15,574
That is the 100% safe treatment
that I am striving for.

299
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:16,575
Yes.

300
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:17,643
However,

301
00:16:18,177 --> 00:16:21,413
the unacceptable has occurred.

302
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:22,848
Yes?

303
00:16:22,915 --> 00:16:25,417
Is "yes" all you can say, you idiot?

304
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:27,853
Yes! I mean, I'm very sorry!

305
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:33,125
So what do you intend to do?

306
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:37,663
I will operate again
and check the situation.

307
00:16:39,465 --> 00:16:41,300
Check the situation?

308
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:43,569
Beds are limited.

309
00:16:43,635 --> 00:16:47,139
Operate again quickly
and discharge him quickly!

310
00:16:50,409 --> 00:16:51,677
Dr. Daimon!

311
00:16:51,744 --> 00:16:53,379
This is an important meeting!

312
00:16:53,445 --> 00:16:55,848
What is the problem, Dr. Daimon?

313
00:16:55,914 --> 00:16:58,183
The video of the surgery was deleted.

314
00:16:58,984 --> 00:17:00,152
What are you talking about?

315
00:17:00,219 --> 00:17:01,387
Covering up your mistake?

316
00:17:01,453 --> 00:17:03,288
That is an inexcusable claim!

317
00:17:03,355 --> 00:17:07,993
Dr. Daimon thinks I am her rival
and she always makes up lies like this.

318
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:09,128
What?

319
00:17:09,661 --> 00:17:12,464
During Kazuo Itsuki's
rectal cancer surgery,

320
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:13,799
a mistake was made,

321
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:15,367
but it was the nurse's fault.

322
00:17:15,434 --> 00:17:17,336
You're blaming it on the nurse?

323
00:17:17,403 --> 00:17:20,806
To protect your reputation,
make a proper explanation.

324
00:17:22,908 --> 00:17:25,044
Soon after starting that surgery,

325
00:17:25,110 --> 00:17:28,113
the temp surgical nurse was useless,
so I got a new one.

326
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:29,181
However,

327
00:17:29,248 --> 00:17:30,816
that nurse was also inexperienced,

328
00:17:31,316 --> 00:17:33,419
<i>and instead of giving me</i>
<i>monofilament as I requested,</i>

329
00:17:33,485 --> 00:17:35,454
<i>she gave me braided suture thread.</i>

330
00:17:35,521 --> 00:17:36,955
That's a critical error.

331
00:17:37,589 --> 00:17:38,857
Because of that,

332
00:17:38,924 --> 00:17:40,993
the rectal anastomosis suturing failed,

333
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,861
leading to descending colon necrosis.

334
00:17:42,928 --> 00:17:44,963
It was you who made the critical error!

335
00:17:45,030 --> 00:17:48,367
There is no way I would make
such a basic mistake as that.

336
00:17:48,434 --> 00:17:49,435
Then,

337
00:17:49,968 --> 00:17:52,704
let us fire that nurse.

338
00:17:52,771 --> 00:17:54,640
He should be the one fired!

339
00:17:54,706 --> 00:18:00,579
Risk hedging should be done
as swiftly as possible.

340
00:18:00,646 --> 00:18:02,748
I don't think you see the true risk.

341
00:18:04,516 --> 00:18:06,351
If you're a doctor, you should know.

342
00:18:07,986 --> 00:18:10,255
The greatest danger to a patient

343
00:18:10,322 --> 00:18:12,691
is a doctor who runs away in a crisis!

344
00:18:38,817 --> 00:18:42,387
I wonder if Mr. Itsuki
will require surgery again.

345
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:48,594
I'm thinking of…

346
00:18:49,561 --> 00:18:54,433
telling them that Dr. Korogi made
a mistake during the anastomosis.

347
00:18:55,234 --> 00:18:56,301
Tell who?

348
00:18:57,836 --> 00:18:59,638
The other surgeons.

349
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:04,042
I'm sure one of them will take my side.

350
00:19:05,711 --> 00:19:06,845
You're too optimistic.

351
00:19:07,613 --> 00:19:09,348
Don't ever trust a doctor.

352
00:19:10,382 --> 00:19:13,352
They're self-interested fools
who rely on their authority.

353
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,955
If the weak ones complain,
they'll just be removed.

354
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:19,925
You really think so?

355
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:23,795
It appears someone deleted
the video of the surgery.

356
00:19:24,363 --> 00:19:25,831
What?

357
00:19:25,898 --> 00:19:28,066
Make sure not to get dragged into it.

358
00:19:29,334 --> 00:19:30,602
Dragged into it?

359
00:19:31,103 --> 00:19:33,138
It's 5 p.m., so I'll be leaving.

360
00:19:40,546 --> 00:19:42,481
MACCHAN DINER

361
00:19:48,654 --> 00:19:49,855
Welcome!

362
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:57,729
MACCHAN DINER
50 YEN OFF

363
00:19:57,796 --> 00:19:58,931
You dropped this.

364
00:19:58,997 --> 00:20:00,866
What brings you all the way here?

365
00:20:00,933 --> 00:20:02,301
What would you like?

366
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:04,436
Sorry. Not today.

367
00:20:05,671 --> 00:20:07,706
What happened in that surgery?

368
00:20:10,142 --> 00:20:12,578
If nothing is done,
that nurse will take the fall.

369
00:20:13,178 --> 00:20:15,180
So Ms. Ohma will be fired?

370
00:20:15,247 --> 00:20:16,348
That's a pity.

371
00:20:16,415 --> 00:20:19,318
You're the only one who can prove
it wasn't her fault.

372
00:20:19,384 --> 00:20:20,619
I refuse.

373
00:20:21,853 --> 00:20:24,556
You're freelance,
so you can understand why.

374
00:20:24,623 --> 00:20:27,025
You know we're rootless wanderers.

375
00:20:28,327 --> 00:20:29,228
What's more,

376
00:20:29,294 --> 00:20:32,030
I am a temp nurse
who works to support doctors.

377
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:36,001
You support doctors?
Even doctors who mess up?

378
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:37,069
At any rate,

379
00:20:37,135 --> 00:20:39,004
I don't want to get involved.

380
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:45,577
What happens in the OR stays in the OR.
Never disobey the surgeon.

381
00:20:46,345 --> 00:20:47,846
Even if the surgeon makes an error,

382
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:50,148
if a temp nurse speaks the truth,

383
00:20:50,215 --> 00:20:52,584
they'll never be hired anywhere again.

384
00:20:52,651 --> 00:20:54,686
They'll be out of work forever.

385
00:20:55,387 --> 00:20:58,557
One must protect one's meal ticket.

386
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:03,996
I didn't like you back then either,

387
00:21:04,062 --> 00:21:06,431
but I did trust you as a nurse.

388
00:21:06,498 --> 00:21:07,766
Why, thank you.

389
00:21:07,833 --> 00:21:08,667
Come now.

390
00:21:09,735 --> 00:21:11,603
You would abandon one of your own?

391
00:21:13,071 --> 00:21:14,206
One of my own?

392
00:21:16,241 --> 00:21:18,410
What happened to you, Dr. Daimon?

393
00:21:18,477 --> 00:21:21,780
You're a lone wolf, but now,
you're supporting a nurse?

394
00:21:23,248 --> 00:21:24,683
Oh…

395
00:21:25,550 --> 00:21:28,887
So you've become
a virtuous person now, have you?

396
00:21:31,657 --> 00:21:34,393
My udon is becoming soft, so please leave.

397
00:21:38,430 --> 00:21:40,299
Then I'll leave you with this.

398
00:21:40,999 --> 00:21:44,303
It's the patients
who ultimately pay the price.

399
00:21:59,251 --> 00:22:03,021
<i>Medical Solutions Division Chief Hachisuka</i>
<i>is now conducting</i>

400
00:22:03,088 --> 00:22:05,257
<i>the chief's rounds.</i>

401
00:22:05,957 --> 00:22:08,927
I wasn't expecting Chief Hachisuka
to do a doctors' procession.

402
00:22:09,461 --> 00:22:11,196
Dr. Korogi is here, too.

403
00:22:11,263 --> 00:22:14,566
I bet he wanted to do the procession
while Acting Director Hiruma is gone.

404
00:22:14,633 --> 00:22:17,703
Chief Hachisuka,
this kind of thing really is nice!

405
00:22:18,403 --> 00:22:21,540
You're so different
from Acting Director Hiruma.

406
00:22:21,606 --> 00:22:23,141
You're speedier.

407
00:22:23,909 --> 00:22:27,579
You are really a dynamic chief!

408
00:22:27,646 --> 00:22:29,948
You call that dynamic?

409
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:33,618
He just wanted to do one
of these doctors' processions.

410
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:37,589
Power corrupts everyone,
even Chief Hachisuka.

411
00:22:45,063 --> 00:22:46,398
Dr. Daimon.

412
00:22:47,299 --> 00:22:49,401
Get in the procession, Dr. Daimon.

413
00:22:49,468 --> 00:22:50,669
I won't.

414
00:22:53,138 --> 00:22:54,272
Out of the way.

415
00:22:56,007 --> 00:22:58,276
Who does she think she is?

416
00:23:00,245 --> 00:23:01,313
Let's continue.

417
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:28,573
Today,

418
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:31,610
Chief Hachisuka will see you personally.

419
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:34,613
He's that important doctor who's on TV.

420
00:23:35,881 --> 00:23:37,816
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

421
00:23:37,883 --> 00:23:39,317
How are you feeling?

422
00:23:40,519 --> 00:23:42,487
It really hurts.

423
00:23:43,889 --> 00:23:46,291
The painkillers aren't working much.

424
00:23:46,358 --> 00:23:48,794
He couldn't sleep again last night.

425
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:53,665
Here, is it?

426
00:23:56,334 --> 00:23:57,569
You'll be fine.

427
00:23:57,636 --> 00:23:59,304
After another surgery,

428
00:23:59,371 --> 00:24:01,873
your C-reactive protein levels
will stabilize.

429
00:24:02,741 --> 00:24:05,043
You have to operate again?

430
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:06,611
This surgery is to be expected.

431
00:24:07,813 --> 00:24:10,882
Post-operative dropsy is common.

432
00:24:12,317 --> 00:24:15,854
Dr. Korogi will perform perfect surgery.

433
00:24:15,921 --> 00:24:17,022
Don't worry.

434
00:24:18,190 --> 00:24:20,125
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

435
00:24:20,192 --> 00:24:21,860
We appreciate this very much.

436
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:28,066
- Straighten your legs.
- Okay.

437
00:24:37,709 --> 00:24:39,244
What do you mean?

438
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:43,849
Chief Hachisuka is saying
he won't make public

439
00:24:43,915 --> 00:24:48,286
that you committed a critical error
during surgery.

440
00:24:48,353 --> 00:24:49,754
But that was…

441
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:50,956
Ordinarily,

442
00:24:51,490 --> 00:24:53,758
you would be summarily dismissed.

443
00:24:56,261 --> 00:24:58,363
Due to paperwork requirements,

444
00:24:58,430 --> 00:25:01,533
you must write a resignation
and submit it.

445
00:25:02,100 --> 00:25:03,702
That is all we need.

446
00:25:03,768 --> 00:25:04,870
You can go now.

447
00:25:08,974 --> 00:25:10,275
Go now!

448
00:25:16,147 --> 00:25:17,849
Fix the problem today.

449
00:25:30,829 --> 00:25:33,298
What's wrong? You look pale.

450
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:37,936
I… was just fired.

451
00:25:43,008 --> 00:25:44,609
Please…

452
00:25:45,477 --> 00:25:48,680
take care of Mr. Itsuki
until he's discharged.

453
00:25:51,449 --> 00:25:53,418
I hope he makes it that far.

454
00:25:55,487 --> 00:25:57,822
That damn Dr. Korogi
is operating again, right?

455
00:25:59,324 --> 00:26:00,158
Yes.

456
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:11,770
This patient could die.

457
00:26:11,836 --> 00:26:13,838
Dr. Daimon, how can you say that?

458
00:26:13,905 --> 00:26:15,574
I mean,

459
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:18,743
all that jerk thinks about
is covering up his own mistakes.

460
00:26:21,479 --> 00:26:23,415
He doesn't operate for the patient's sake,

461
00:26:23,949 --> 00:26:25,884
but for his own.

462
00:26:38,229 --> 00:26:39,598
The morning of his surgery,

463
00:26:41,499 --> 00:26:42,834
this is what he told me.

464
00:26:43,501 --> 00:26:46,171
<i>Did you sleep well last night?</i>

465
00:26:46,237 --> 00:26:48,073
No, not really.

466
00:26:48,807 --> 00:26:51,676
This is the first time
I've ever had surgery.

467
00:26:52,711 --> 00:26:54,613
He doesn't look it,
but he's such a coward.

468
00:26:54,679 --> 00:26:56,181
Don't worry.

469
00:26:56,247 --> 00:26:59,618
When you wake up, it will all be over.
Then you just get better.

470
00:27:00,585 --> 00:27:02,087
I sure hope so.

471
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:05,957
Do you like hot springs?

472
00:27:06,024 --> 00:27:07,025
PRIVATE HOT SPRING

473
00:27:07,092 --> 00:27:09,427
My husband is a magazine writer.

474
00:27:09,494 --> 00:27:11,296
All his articles are about hot springs.

475
00:27:11,363 --> 00:27:13,565
Oh, is that right?

476
00:27:14,366 --> 00:27:15,200
HOT SPRING REPORTER KAZUO ITSUKI

477
00:27:15,266 --> 00:27:16,568
I love this work.

478
00:27:17,435 --> 00:27:20,271
I would prefer not to be fitted
with a colostomy bag.

479
00:27:21,206 --> 00:27:24,175
It would make it difficult
to use the hot springs.

480
00:27:25,510 --> 00:27:27,879
I'll make sure the doctor knows that.

481
00:27:28,647 --> 00:27:30,048
Thank you.

482
00:27:34,019 --> 00:27:35,954
Mr. Itsuki said that?

483
00:27:38,923 --> 00:27:40,859
So you're kind to the patients, huh?

484
00:27:41,826 --> 00:27:44,262
And did he say anything else?

485
00:27:48,299 --> 00:27:49,501
Well…

486
00:27:50,835 --> 00:27:52,837
I asked about his medical history.

487
00:27:54,139 --> 00:27:56,141
A year ago,

488
00:27:57,208 --> 00:28:00,011
he got hemorrhoids
and got an injection in his anus.

489
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:03,815
That's what made it so hard.

490
00:28:04,683 --> 00:28:07,452
Then that damn Dr. Korogi
messed up the anastomosis.

491
00:28:19,297 --> 00:28:21,232
What a nice smell!

492
00:28:21,299 --> 00:28:22,701
Let's see.

493
00:28:22,767 --> 00:28:25,170
I hope the meat didn't fall apart.

494
00:28:26,271 --> 00:28:28,840
It's been stewing for three days,
after all.

495
00:28:28,907 --> 00:28:30,341
Are you listening, Michiko?

496
00:28:30,408 --> 00:28:31,943
No, I can tell you're not.

497
00:28:32,010 --> 00:28:36,281
I wrapped it in a net
to keep it from falling apart.

498
00:28:39,551 --> 00:28:41,186
It worked!

499
00:28:41,252 --> 00:28:46,224
The beef cheek stewed in red wine
turned out perfect!

500
00:28:46,291 --> 00:28:48,860
Ben Casey and Gannon, look!

501
00:28:48,927 --> 00:28:51,262
The meat didn't fall apart at all!

502
00:28:51,329 --> 00:28:54,165
- Oh, wow! That looks delicious!
- It sure does!

503
00:28:54,966 --> 00:28:56,434
How come it didn't fall apart?

504
00:28:56,501 --> 00:28:57,502
Like I said,

505
00:28:57,569 --> 00:28:59,838
I wrapped it in a net.

506
00:28:59,904 --> 00:29:01,940
See how it has a fishnet pattern on it?

507
00:29:03,475 --> 00:29:05,944
See? Looks good, doesn't it?

508
00:29:06,010 --> 00:29:08,513
I know the kind of things you like.

509
00:29:14,486 --> 00:29:16,521
You're the surgical nurse again?

510
00:29:17,555 --> 00:29:20,391
I am so sorry.
You'll have to put up with me again.

511
00:29:20,458 --> 00:29:24,095
We're short on nurses
and Ms. Ohma was suddenly fired,

512
00:29:24,162 --> 00:29:26,097
so this temp nurse is all there is.

513
00:29:27,265 --> 00:29:28,700
I guess I've got no choice.

514
00:29:33,338 --> 00:29:37,142
BP 132 over 85, pulse 70, normal sinus.

515
00:29:37,208 --> 00:29:38,543
SECOND LAPAROSCOPIC SURGERY

516
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:40,345
Aren't you a temp, too?

517
00:29:41,379 --> 00:29:42,413
Yes.

518
00:29:43,081 --> 00:29:45,183
There sure are a lot of you lately.

519
00:29:45,250 --> 00:29:49,320
But you're one of the easier temps
to get along with.

520
00:29:49,387 --> 00:29:52,657
The worst one is that lady temp doctor.

521
00:29:53,658 --> 00:29:54,492
Doctor,

522
00:29:55,026 --> 00:29:56,628
hurry up and begin.

523
00:29:58,663 --> 00:29:59,998
Don't give me orders!

524
00:30:01,399 --> 00:30:04,702
Besides, with me at the helm,
we'll be done in no time.

525
00:30:05,703 --> 00:30:07,739
How about a drink after surgery?

526
00:30:08,406 --> 00:30:09,641
After surgery?

527
00:30:11,609 --> 00:30:12,610
Sure.

528
00:30:13,211 --> 00:30:15,280
Then let's finish this fast.

529
00:30:15,346 --> 00:30:16,614
Coop…

530
00:30:18,449 --> 00:30:20,952
Didn't I tell you to wait for my orders?

531
00:30:53,017 --> 00:30:53,985
Head Doctor…

532
00:30:55,253 --> 00:30:57,121
Pus throughout the abdominal cavity.

533
00:30:57,989 --> 00:30:59,557
Don't tell me that! I can see!

534
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:06,030
We can't see the failed suture
of the rectal anastomosis.

535
00:31:06,097 --> 00:31:08,366
Quit explaining everything!

536
00:31:11,669 --> 00:31:13,071
Doctor, what will we do?

537
00:31:16,574 --> 00:31:19,878
- We'll cut him open.
- What? We'll open him up now?

538
00:31:20,411 --> 00:31:22,447
Lower digestive tract
may have been punctured.

539
00:31:22,513 --> 00:31:23,882
We must open his abdomen.

540
00:31:23,948 --> 00:31:25,884
Sorry, Dr. Jonouchi.
Rain check on that date.

541
00:31:25,950 --> 00:31:28,953
- Forget that! Find the puncture now!
- I know!

542
00:31:42,500 --> 00:31:44,669
Where's the puncture?

543
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:50,508
We'll have to remove
the necrotic descending colon.

544
00:31:52,176 --> 00:31:53,444
Stay calm.

545
00:31:53,511 --> 00:31:55,880
You should re-evaluate
the surgical technique.

546
00:31:56,381 --> 00:31:58,316
The surgical technique?

547
00:31:58,383 --> 00:32:01,352
How dare a temp nurse like you
talk as if you know

548
00:32:01,419 --> 00:32:03,187
anything about surgical technique!

549
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:11,229
BP down to 60!

550
00:32:11,729 --> 00:32:13,364
LOW BLOOD PRESSURE ALARM

551
00:32:18,236 --> 00:32:20,204
Attach a drain to the vesicorectal pouch

552
00:32:20,271 --> 00:32:21,739
and construct a permanent stoma.

553
00:32:21,806 --> 00:32:24,475
We can't. The patient does not want
a permanent stoma.

554
00:32:24,542 --> 00:32:25,677
Who cares about that!

555
00:32:25,743 --> 00:32:28,079
Mr. Itsuki wants to continue
writing about hot springs.

556
00:32:28,146 --> 00:32:30,848
Safe surgery is more important
than quality of life!

557
00:32:30,915 --> 00:32:32,517
Prep a permanent stoma, stat!

558
00:32:32,583 --> 00:32:33,484
Yes, sir!

559
00:32:33,551 --> 00:32:35,853
There are other options.
Put yourself in his shoes!

560
00:32:35,920 --> 00:32:37,422
Find a way to avoid doing this.

561
00:32:37,488 --> 00:32:39,324
Who do you think you are, you temp?

562
00:32:40,858 --> 00:32:42,226
Time out!

563
00:32:42,293 --> 00:32:43,494
What?

564
00:32:45,463 --> 00:32:49,300
We don't need
incompetent doctors like you!

565
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:52,203
Agreed!

566
00:32:52,770 --> 00:32:54,405
Replace the surgeon!

567
00:32:57,942 --> 00:32:59,243
Dr. Daimon!

568
00:32:59,310 --> 00:33:01,579
- What are you doing here?
- Out of the way!

569
00:33:02,213 --> 00:33:03,214
Oh, man.

570
00:33:03,281 --> 00:33:05,149
I figured it would be like this.

571
00:33:05,216 --> 00:33:07,719
What? I thought you were fired!

572
00:33:07,785 --> 00:33:09,921
- Out, both of you!
- No!

573
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:12,123
I won't let another error be made
on this patient.

574
00:33:12,190 --> 00:33:13,791
That was your mistake!

575
00:33:13,858 --> 00:33:16,027
- You're still saying that?
- I made no mistake!

576
00:33:16,094 --> 00:33:18,162
November 6th, 10 a.m.

577
00:33:18,229 --> 00:33:20,198
Dr. Korogi conducted

578
00:33:20,264 --> 00:33:23,001
a laparoscopic lower anterior
resection in this OR.

579
00:33:26,070 --> 00:33:28,006
It's hard.

580
00:33:28,072 --> 00:33:31,142
<i>The patient underwent internal</i>
<i>hemorrhoid hardening treatment,</i>

581
00:33:31,209 --> 00:33:34,445
<i>so his rectal wall was hard,</i>
<i>making anastomosis difficult.</i>

582
00:33:34,512 --> 00:33:37,148
<i>So Dr. Korogi forcefully used</i>
<i>the automated anastomosis device.</i>

583
00:33:37,215 --> 00:33:38,649
See?

584
00:33:38,716 --> 00:33:40,118
That did it.

585
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:43,121
<i>Then additional suturing was required.</i>

586
00:33:43,187 --> 00:33:46,190
Arrogantly shoving instruments in my face
is throwing me off!

587
00:33:46,257 --> 00:33:48,259
Where's the new surgical nurse?

588
00:33:48,326 --> 00:33:51,629
<i>Dr. Korogi had the scrub nurse</i>
<i>replaced by nurse Masako Ohma.</i>

589
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:52,897
4-0 braided.

590
00:33:52,964 --> 00:33:54,499
What? Braided?

591
00:33:54,565 --> 00:33:56,100
Don't you want monofilament?

592
00:33:56,167 --> 00:33:58,436
He asked for 4-0 braided suture thread.

593
00:33:58,503 --> 00:34:01,706
Nurse Ohma asked to make sure
he didn't want monofilament,

594
00:34:01,773 --> 00:34:04,442
whose single strand is less likely
to damage tissue

595
00:34:04,509 --> 00:34:07,779
than the multiple strands
of braided suture thread.

596
00:34:08,413 --> 00:34:09,414
However,

597
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:13,051
<i>Dr. Korogi sutured with the braided suture</i>
<i>easier to use</i>

598
00:34:13,117 --> 00:34:15,319
<i>even with its increased risk</i>
<i>of post-operative infection.</i>

599
00:34:16,654 --> 00:34:17,822
In other words,

600
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:22,060
Dr. Korogi could clearly anticipate
the failure of the suturing.

601
00:34:23,227 --> 00:34:24,762
There you have it.

602
00:34:25,329 --> 00:34:28,232
Mistake one, forcefully anastomosing.

603
00:34:28,299 --> 00:34:31,102
Mistake two,
using the wrong suture thread.

604
00:34:31,169 --> 00:34:33,438
Mistake three, slipshod suturing.

605
00:34:33,504 --> 00:34:35,073
You're a mistake bonanza!

606
00:34:35,139 --> 00:34:36,274
Those are all lies!

607
00:34:36,340 --> 00:34:37,708
Where's your proof?

608
00:34:37,775 --> 00:34:39,610
I've had enough of your fantasies!

609
00:34:39,677 --> 00:34:41,746
And I've had enough of you!

610
00:34:41,813 --> 00:34:43,714
We've got proof right here!

611
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:47,185
SURGEON HIROSHI KOROGI

612
00:34:49,487 --> 00:34:50,521
4-0 BRAIDED

613
00:34:50,588 --> 00:34:52,757
INSTEAD OF 4-0 MONOFILAMENT

614
00:34:53,858 --> 00:34:55,993
If the suturing failed,

615
00:34:56,060 --> 00:34:57,462
then just suture it again!

616
00:34:57,528 --> 00:34:59,464
That's not enough!

617
00:34:59,964 --> 00:35:02,633
Inflammation is so severe,
suturing is impossible.

618
00:35:02,700 --> 00:35:05,203
Intestinal fluids will leak
from the puncture again.

619
00:35:07,205 --> 00:35:09,507
- Net!
- "Net?"

620
00:35:09,574 --> 00:35:12,310
- What are you talking about?
- I'll wrap it with greater omentum.

621
00:35:15,646 --> 00:35:16,647
I see.

622
00:35:16,714 --> 00:35:18,716
I'll remove the necrotic descending colon,

623
00:35:18,783 --> 00:35:21,886
then use what's left of the rectum
to redo the anastomosis.

624
00:35:21,953 --> 00:35:23,187
That won't--

625
00:35:23,254 --> 00:35:25,656
I'll wrap the new anastomosis
in greater omentum

626
00:35:25,723 --> 00:35:26,724
to prevent leakage.

627
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:28,526
That's what I mean by "net"!

628
00:35:30,194 --> 00:35:31,662
Surgical technique change!

629
00:35:32,530 --> 00:35:34,198
- Out of the way!
- Ouch!

630
00:35:36,868 --> 00:35:38,035
Oh, dear.

631
00:35:38,102 --> 00:35:41,239
As a mere temp nurse, I am terribly sorry.

632
00:35:44,375 --> 00:35:45,376
You…

633
00:35:45,877 --> 00:35:48,713
I can't operate with you savages!

634
00:35:48,779 --> 00:35:50,481
You're running away again?

635
00:35:50,548 --> 00:35:52,116
You could at least assist.

636
00:35:54,852 --> 00:35:56,721
If you don't attach a permanent stoma,

637
00:35:57,488 --> 00:35:58,923
this will fail!

638
00:35:59,724 --> 00:36:01,626
I think you know this already.

639
00:36:01,692 --> 00:36:05,363
I will not fail.

640
00:36:08,132 --> 00:36:09,300
Let's go!

641
00:36:09,367 --> 00:36:10,201
Yes, sir.

642
00:36:10,968 --> 00:36:12,403
Bov…

643
00:36:30,755 --> 00:36:33,824
That must be that temp nurse.

644
00:36:49,307 --> 00:36:50,308
Amazing…

645
00:37:02,887 --> 00:37:05,289
After this, I'll trim the anastomosis.

646
00:37:05,356 --> 00:37:07,592
I've prepped a right-angle mosquito clamp.

647
00:37:07,658 --> 00:37:08,993
I'll ablate the greater omentum.

648
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:11,662
I'll prep six vein clamps
for constructing the flap.

649
00:37:25,610 --> 00:37:27,178
- Well done.
- Well done.

650
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:29,547
Dr. Daimon, well done.

651
00:37:29,614 --> 00:37:30,615
Well done.

652
00:37:30,681 --> 00:37:34,285
Ms. Nasuda, I will work hard
to be a surgical nurse like you.

653
00:37:34,952 --> 00:37:36,220
You're too inexperienced.

654
00:37:36,287 --> 00:37:37,688
She's scary.

655
00:37:37,755 --> 00:37:39,457
Surgeon, get out!

656
00:37:39,523 --> 00:37:40,591
What?

657
00:37:41,158 --> 00:37:43,594
The rest of the work is for us to do.

658
00:37:45,029 --> 00:37:47,231
I know.

659
00:37:52,803 --> 00:37:55,206
She has some real guts.

660
00:38:23,301 --> 00:38:26,003
- This feels so good!
- This is awesome!

661
00:38:27,271 --> 00:38:29,540
- What a great morning.
- Morning is nice.

662
00:38:29,607 --> 00:38:30,775
- Hey!
- Hey!

663
00:38:33,177 --> 00:38:35,913
Isn't it hot in there?

664
00:38:39,750 --> 00:38:42,186
Ouch! That's hot!

665
00:38:42,253 --> 00:38:44,288
That's so hot!

666
00:38:44,355 --> 00:38:46,857
The perfect temperature.

667
00:38:46,924 --> 00:38:48,492
You're kidding.

668
00:38:48,559 --> 00:38:49,760
That's hot!

669
00:38:49,827 --> 00:38:52,897
- She's totally faking that she likes it.
- For sure.

670
00:38:52,963 --> 00:38:53,864
I'll try it.

671
00:39:02,039 --> 00:39:04,775
Katsu curry in the morning.
It really warms you!

672
00:39:04,842 --> 00:39:06,110
It sure does.

673
00:39:06,177 --> 00:39:07,178
Hey?

674
00:39:07,878 --> 00:39:09,313
Aren't you having udon today?

675
00:39:11,048 --> 00:39:13,784
I get quite hungry after a good operation.

676
00:39:16,654 --> 00:39:18,356
Like you, Ms. Daimon.

677
00:39:19,123 --> 00:39:21,125
- This is great!
- It sure is.

678
00:39:24,662 --> 00:39:26,263
Sir, take this one, too.

679
00:39:26,330 --> 00:39:28,165
- Sure thing.
- What's that?

680
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:32,803
She leaves them with me
after every operation.

681
00:39:32,870 --> 00:39:34,438
She sure works hard.

682
00:39:34,505 --> 00:39:36,874
Hey, can I have a look at it?

683
00:39:36,941 --> 00:39:38,209
Sure.

684
00:39:44,415 --> 00:39:45,282
What?

685
00:39:46,283 --> 00:39:47,618
This is amazing!

686
00:39:48,285 --> 00:39:50,855
If there's a mistake when a nurse
obeys a doctor's orders,

687
00:39:50,921 --> 00:39:52,723
the nurse can be sued in the US.

688
00:39:52,790 --> 00:39:54,759
So this is to protect yourself?

689
00:39:55,559 --> 00:39:56,560
In Japan, too,

690
00:39:56,627 --> 00:39:58,929
doctors are always making mistakes.

691
00:39:58,996 --> 00:40:02,600
I absolutely refuse
to clean up their mistakes.

692
00:40:04,468 --> 00:40:06,670
I never make mistakes.

693
00:40:12,276 --> 00:40:14,211
- What?
- Here you are, sir.

694
00:40:15,379 --> 00:40:16,347
Enjoy

695
00:40:16,414 --> 00:40:17,748
- Thanks.
- Thanks.

696
00:40:17,815 --> 00:40:21,218
MEDICAL SOLUTIONS DIVISION CHIEF
RYUTARO HACHISUKA

697
00:40:21,285 --> 00:40:22,820
It was completed without issue.

698
00:40:22,887 --> 00:40:25,923
The prognosis is that he'll be discharged
very quickly.

699
00:40:26,690 --> 00:40:30,694
That was truly a magnificent surgery.

700
00:40:31,762 --> 00:40:32,830
Yes!

701
00:40:32,897 --> 00:40:34,265
However,

702
00:40:34,865 --> 00:40:36,534
you have disappointed me.

703
00:40:37,101 --> 00:40:38,569
What?

704
00:40:48,712 --> 00:40:51,916
Michiko Daimon forced her way
into this surgery!

705
00:40:51,982 --> 00:40:53,250
I made no mistakes!

706
00:40:56,287 --> 00:40:57,721
I made no mistakes!

707
00:40:59,990 --> 00:41:01,625
I didn't make a mistake.

708
00:41:01,692 --> 00:41:03,427
Chief Hachisuka,

709
00:41:03,494 --> 00:41:05,262
Kambara Doctor Referral Agency is here.

710
00:41:05,329 --> 00:41:07,765
Thank you for doing business with us.

711
00:41:08,399 --> 00:41:13,571
Oh, my. Dr. Korogi,
you're looking awfully pale.

712
00:41:15,039 --> 00:41:17,641
Well, Chief Hachisuka.

713
00:41:17,708 --> 00:41:21,946
I've brought the bill
for last night's overtime surgery.

714
00:41:22,746 --> 00:41:25,049
Is that the famous melon?

715
00:41:25,115 --> 00:41:26,283
Yes.

716
00:41:26,984 --> 00:41:28,152
This is a melon.

717
00:41:31,856 --> 00:41:33,491
This is the bill.

718
00:41:39,396 --> 00:41:40,698
ANESTHETIST JONOUCHI

719
00:41:40,764 --> 00:41:41,799
SURGEON DAIMON

720
00:41:41,866 --> 00:41:42,867
That's expensive!

721
00:41:43,767 --> 00:41:45,102
Unbelievable.

722
00:41:48,472 --> 00:41:52,877
When observing surgery
performed with exquisite talent,

723
00:41:52,943 --> 00:41:55,012
it leaves an impression on your heart.

724
00:41:55,079 --> 00:41:56,146
Yes, it does.

725
00:41:56,213 --> 00:41:57,414
However,

726
00:41:57,948 --> 00:42:02,186
Dr. Daimon used the OR without permission

727
00:42:02,253 --> 00:42:04,622
to conduct this surgery.

728
00:42:05,322 --> 00:42:07,725
We will pay for this.

729
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:11,028
But not this.

730
00:42:11,729 --> 00:42:13,264
You're kidding.

731
00:42:17,568 --> 00:42:19,336
Then…

732
00:42:21,038 --> 00:42:24,775
I will ask you
to handle this one, Dr. Korogi.

733
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:26,677
Here you go.

734
00:42:35,052 --> 00:42:37,288
SURGICAL FEES FOR DR. DAIMON

735
00:42:42,893 --> 00:42:43,961
Dr. Daimon!

736
00:42:44,962 --> 00:42:47,498
I got my job back.

737
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:49,300
- That's great.
- Thank you.

738
00:42:49,366 --> 00:42:50,467
Michiko!

739
00:42:51,702 --> 00:42:53,771
What are you so happy about?

740
00:42:53,837 --> 00:42:56,073
Where's Nurse X?

741
00:42:56,140 --> 00:42:57,508
"Nurse X?"

742
00:42:57,575 --> 00:43:00,210
You know. The temp nurse.

743
00:43:00,744 --> 00:43:02,880
Let's get her working for us right away.

744
00:43:02,947 --> 00:43:07,184
With her around, my doctor agency
will be firm as a rock.

745
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:10,054
- Ms. Nasuda has left.
- What?

746
00:43:10,120 --> 00:43:12,489
Her contract ended and she left just now.

747
00:43:12,556 --> 00:43:14,792
Are you kidding? Which way did she go?

748
00:43:14,858 --> 00:43:17,194
Where's that nurse? Where's Nurse X?

749
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:20,064
This way? You won't get away!

750
00:43:34,345 --> 00:43:38,649
There might actually be doctors
who can be trusted.

751
00:43:43,253 --> 00:43:46,991
Goodbye, Dr. Daimon.

752
00:44:21,158 --> 00:44:22,259
She left.

753
00:44:27,665 --> 00:44:29,199
<i>She hates groups,</i>

754
00:44:29,266 --> 00:44:30,534
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

755
00:44:30,601 --> 00:44:32,369
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

756
00:44:32,870 --> 00:44:36,373
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

757
00:44:36,440 --> 00:44:38,142
<i>to work her way up.</i>

758
00:44:38,208 --> 00:44:40,377
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

759
00:44:40,444 --> 00:44:44,014
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

760
00:44:44,081 --> 00:44:45,549
<i>You'll make a mistake.</i>

761
00:44:45,616 --> 00:44:48,318
I'm no longer a doctor who sticks
with the crowd and says "Yes, sir."

762
00:44:48,385 --> 00:44:49,987
He's Asia's wealthiest man!

763
00:44:50,054 --> 00:44:52,423
<i>These two tumors</i>
<i>really are quite a problem.</i>

764
00:44:52,489 --> 00:44:53,424
Crap!

765
00:44:53,490 --> 00:44:55,159
Miracles don't happen in surgery.

766
00:44:55,225 --> 00:44:58,262
Michiko Daimon is no longer needed, right?

767
00:44:58,328 --> 00:44:59,329
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
